    "problem": "Climate models struggled to explain the 'global-warming hiatus,' a period since 1998 where observed atmospheric warming stalled in stark contrast to projections, challenging scientists to identify where the excess heat was going, with evidence pointing towards deep-ocean absorption driven by natural variability in the Pacific.",
    "method": "The proposed explanation for the global-warming hiatus is that a cool phase of a natural ocean cycle, the Pacific Decadal Oscillation, has caused the deep ocean to absorb excess heat, stalling the rise in atmospheric temperatures.",
    "task": "The task is to explain the \"global-warming hiatus\"\u2014a slowdown in rising atmospheric temperatures since 1998\u2014by investigating where the \"missing heat\" has gone, with a primary focus on its absorption by natural cycles in the Pacific Ocean.",
