            "target_entity_instance": "central Pacific",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "This variation in ocean temperature, known as the Pacific Decadal Oscillation (PDO), may be a crucial piece of the hiatus puzzle. The cycle reverses every 15\u201330 years, and in its positive phase, the oscillation favours El Ni\u00f1o, which tends to warm the atmosphere (see \u2018The fickle ocean\u2019). After a couple of decades of releasing heat from the eastern and central Pacific, the region cools and enters the negative phase of the PDO.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "La Ni\u00f1a",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Equator",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "This state tends towards La Ni\u00f1a, which brings cool waters up from the depths along the Equator and tends to cool the planet.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "tropical trade winds",
            "source_entity_type": "Ocean_Circulation",
            "relation": "OBSERVED_IN_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "eastern equatorial region",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Their study documents how tropical trade winds associated with La Ni\u00f1a conditions help to drive warm water westward and, ultimately, deep into the ocean, while promoting the upwelling of cool waters along the eastern equatorial region.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "tropical trade winds",
